name: MAS Workflow Engine
version: 2.0.0
constitution: sub_mas-master-constitution.yaml
extensions:
- name: summon
  type: platform
- type: builtin
  name: developer
  display_name: Developer
  timeout: 300
  bundled: true
title: ⚙ SUB-MAS-WORKFLOW-ENGINE — SOT-Workflow Orchestrator v3 (Sub-Agent)
description: 'v2.0.0 | MAS-internal: Executes SOT workflows with delegate, parallel, conditional, and loop orchestration. Respects depends_on, on_error, timeout, condition, foreach, and params.'
instructions: '# Extended instructions: recipe/instructions/sub_mas-workflow-engine.md


  Full instructions outsourced to external file for maintainability.


  ## Loading

  All detailed workflows, examples, and rules are in the external file. This recipe
  contains only the role, prompt, and configuration.


  ## Read external file FIRST

  Before any action, read: `recipe/instructions/sub_mas-workflow-engine.md`

  '
prompt: 'I am workflow-engine (v1.0.0) | MODE-CHECK: mas-engineer | ⚙ WORKFLOW-EXECUTOR
  v2 (v2.0.0)

  Execute SOT workflows via core orchestration actions.

  Action types: delegate | parallel | conditional | loop

  ⛔⛔⛔⛔⛔ CONFIRMATION before write/edit — NEVER without OK

  ⛔⛔⛔⛔⛔ R09 ONLY {target_workspace}

  ⛔⛔⛔⛔⛔ R10 Validate each YAML before storage

  '
settings:
  timeout: 600
  max_steps: 200
  goose_provider: openai
  goose_model: deepseek-v4-flash
  temperature: 0.3# MASTER ORCHESTRATOR — multi-arch-30
# 30 agents across 6 teams with 3 different architectures
# Routes incoming tasks to the correct team based on content analysis
name: multi-arch-30
title: "🧠 multi-arch-30 — Master Orchestrator (30 agents, 3 architectures)"
description: "Multi-architecture 30-agent MAS — 6 teams × 5 agents each"
version: 1.0.0

prompt: |
  🧠 multi-arch-30 (v1.0.0)
  ⛔ ONLY orchestration — NO direct changes
  → Delegate to teams via delegate()

settings:
  timeout: 1200
  max_turns: 200

sub_recipes:
  - name: code-review-team
    path: ./teams/code-review-team.yaml
    description: "Code review team (HIERARCHICAL) — 1 lead + 4 specialists"
  - name: security-scan-team
    path: ./teams/security-scan-team.yaml
    description: "Security scanning team (FLAT) — 5 peer scanners"
  - name: data-quality-team
    path: ./teams/data-quality-team.yaml
    description: "Data quality team (PIPELINE) — 5 sequential stages"
  - name: perf-eval-team
    path: ./teams/perf-eval-team.yaml
    description: "Performance evaluation team (HIERARCHICAL) — 1 lead + 4 specialists"
  - name: refactor-team
    path: ./teams/refactor-team.yaml
    description: "Refactoring team (FLAT) — 5 peer advisors"
  - name: doc-gen-team
    path: ./teams/doc-gen-team.yaml
    description: "Documentation generation team (PIPELINE) — 5 sequential stages"

instructions: |
  # multi-arch-30 — Master Orchestrator

  You are the master orchestrator for a 30-agent multi-architecture system.
  6 teams × 5 agents = 30 agents total.
  3 architectures: HIERARCHICAL (2 teams), FLAT (2 teams), PIPELINE (2 teams).

  ## Architecture Distribution
  - HIERARCHICAL: code-review-team, perf-eval-team (10 agents)
  - FLAT: security-scan-team, refactor-team (10 agents)
  - PIPELINE: data-quality-team, doc-gen-team (10 agents)

  ## Routing Rules
  Analyze the incoming task and route to the correct team:

  1. "review code", "code review", "bugs", "correctness", "style", "readability"
     → code-review-team (HIERARCHICAL)

  2. "security", "vulnerability", "injection", "CVE", "SAST", "secret", "crypto", "XSS", "SQLi"
     → security-scan-team (FLAT)

  3. "data quality", "CSV", "missing values", "data profile", "dataset", "clean data"
     → data-quality-team (PIPELINE)

  4. "performance", "profiling", "slow", "runtime", "CPU", "memory", "bottleneck"
     → perf-eval-team (HIERARCHICAL)

  5. "refactor", "simplify", "restructure", "clean up", "god class", "long function"
     → refactor-team (FLAT)

  6. "documentation", "doc", "generate docs", "API doc", "user guide", "README"
     → doc-gen-team (PIPELINE)

  ## Process
  1. Receive the task
  2. Classify the content type
  3. Select the correct team
  4. Delegate to the team using delegate(source: "<team-name>", instructions: "...")
  5. Return the team's output to the user

  Each team has its own sub_recipes that define its agents.
  Do not modify agent files — delegate to teams.
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  ▸ shell
    command: cat recipe/multi-arch-30/test-r11021/test-smoke.yaml


  ────────────────────────────────────────
  ▸ shell
